title: Infoblox: Deployed service status
agents: infoblox_csp
catalog: cloud/infoblox
license: GPLv2
distribution: mkp
description:
 Reports the status of a service deployed on a NIOS-X server, such as DNS,
 DHCP, DNS Forwarding Proxy, NTP or Data Connector.

 The service is {OK} while the status is started, {WARN} while starting or
 stopping, and {CRIT} when stopped or in error. Every mapping is
 configurable.

 The details include the version, the service name as held in the portal,
 how long the service has been in its current state, and when it was last
 upgraded. Where the portal supplies an error payload it is decoded and
 shown, including the failing container name and exit code.

 Versions are reported but never alarmed on, because Infoblox controls
 service versions and applies updates automatically.

discovery:
 One service is created for each service deployed on the server.

item:
 The service type as Infoblox names it in the portal, for example DNS,
 DHCP, NTP or DNS Forwarding Proxy. A service type unknown to this
 extension appears as the raw value in upper case. If a server ever reports
 two services of the same type, every member of that group is suffixed with
 its service name so that items stay unique and stable.
